# Medical tourism site: core

Static information site for international patients. Astro 7 (SSG), TypeScript strict, Tailwind CSS 4, Markdown/MDX content collections, Netlify. No backend.

## Stack
- Pages, layouts, and content UI are `.astro` components. React `.tsx` only for interactive islands with a `client:*` directive.
- Every page uses `MainLayout`. Routes are files in `src/pages/`. Nav items live in `src/lib/navigation.ts`.
- Bilingual, English and Myanmar: every page, UI string, and article is created in both languages (`.cursor/rules/i18n.mdc`).
- Style with Tailwind classes and the tokens in the `@theme` block of `src/styles/global.css`.
- Do not invent colors, font sizes, breakpoints, button variants, or new shared components when an existing one fits.

## Design guidelines
`docs/design/` holds the design rules. Before changing UI, styles, or page templates, read `docs/design/README.md` and only the topic file you need (typography, color, buttons, navigation, cards, layout, content, languages). Do not read the whole folder.

## Top-layer changes keep docs in sync
A change is top-layer if later pages are expected to copy it:
- The `@theme` block, `base` layer, or `.prose-content` in `src/styles/global.css`
- Props or visual behavior of `Button`, `Container`, `Header`, `Footer`, `ArticleCard`, `MainLayout`
- The navigation model in `src/lib/navigation.ts`
- Locales, URL scheme, or translation structure (`src/i18n/ui.ts`, `astro.config.mjs` `i18n`)
- A new shared component, breakpoint rule, or page/content template

In the same task, before reporting done:
1. Update the matching `docs/design/*.md` file.
2. Update `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` if a do or don't changed.
3. Add a dated entry to `docs/design/changelog.md`.
4. If it contradicts `docs/design/principles.md`, say so to the user and update it deliberately.

Not top-layer: article copy, one-off sections built from existing components, bugfixes restoring documented behavior.

## Verify
Run `npm run check` and `npm run lint` after code changes.
